ift the other one directly  upwards with this movement you're  stretching the hamstrings while keeping  the back in a much flatter position  moreover you're actually employing  strength to train real mobility by  engaging the working muscles and  relaxing the antagonists  this is what mobility really boils down  to control over your nervous system and  awareness of the entire body and it's  not just a stretch then it's actually a  strength challenge and you might find  that your legs really burn much more  than you're expecting and noah is this  kind of training more effective than in  bar class  so bar class is training against a bar  for ballet focused controller mobility a  lot of this involves supporting your  weight ever so slightly on a bar hence  the name while performing a range of leg  extensions lateral and forwards lifts  with control  in many cases you'll then draw tiny  circles with the extended legs for 30  seconds reverse direction and place back  down one big focus in bar training and  that applies to a lot of movements  whether it's a leg lift or something  like a plie is pelvis control and this  is once again a really under utilized  aspect of strength and performance being  able to get your pelvis into the correct  position is crucial for so many  different exercises and it can lead to  injury if you don't know how to do this  but unfortunately that's exactly the  problem so many of us have no idea how  to control our pelvis because we're  sitting on our butts all day we end up  putting our spines into these unusual  positions that often result in an  anterior pelvic tilt and we've lost the  mind muscle connection to allow  ourselves to move our spines the way  that we really need to  in bar training you're encouraged to  tuck the pelvis underneath during  movements like the plie and the leg lift  and this helps to maintain a neutral  spine thereby creating poise and  alignment to make balance much easier  and to help you jump higher and of  course it looks nice as well now there  are some that say that focusing too much  on tucking the pelvis like this can  actually be a bad thing if you're  someone who does a lot of ballet but for  the majority of us it's hardly going to  be because most of us have anterior  pelvic tilt the exact opposite problem  so this is just a perfect example of how  ballet and dance in general can teach  you to be more aware of your body and to  reawaken that mind muscle connection to  improve the quality of your movement to  reduce injury and to perform better and  of course this type of training also  requires balance and stability on the  supporting leg especially if you also  practice it without the bar  this might feel like a flexibility  routine but you'll build real strength  and control here too  [Music]  and anyway everyone should aspire to  graceful precise movement  black widow movement  these extensions are performed from a  range of different positions in fact  this is true of most ballet moves there  are five basic ballet positions  literally named first second third  fourth and fifth each of which involve  turning the feet out to varying degrees  tight tips can be a huge issue for some  people and even make it impossible to  get into a deep squat without collapsing  the knees  these drills will prevent injury and  allow you to express power from a range  of different positions i recently  recommended performing the sumo squat  with leg lift to work both abductors and  adductors to build simultaneous strength  and mobility  but another similar movement from ballet  is the standard plie squat plie  literally means bending the knees and  this is a squatting movement with the  legs and feet turned out you can also  perform a plie squat which is  essentially the same movement adapted  into an exercise and in the plie squat  what you're going to be doing is placing  your feet just wider than shoulder width  apart and turning your toes outwards  about 45 degrees you're not going to be  turning at the ankles though or at the  knees you're going to be turning at the  hip work on this not only will you be  able to do those awesome black widow  landings not only will you be able to  kick super high but you'll also actually  improve your regular squat as you can  get your legs a little bit wider and  therefore get deeper into the squat at  the same time this is going to work on  your ankle mobility and strengthen you  in places that you're probably not used  to even if you normally have a massive  squat this is probably something that  you're going to really feel because it's  just not something that you're used to  at the same time we need to focus on our  torso and keeping our back nice and  extended and upright and our neck  elongated you want to imagine that  there's a piece of string coming from  the top of your head that you're a  puppet and someone is pulling that  straight upwards this is going to  improve your posture and your poise and  it's actually going to make you feel  lighter on your feet it's not just about  looking more aesthetic it'll actually  improve your jump height and your  general ability to move quickly and  lightly this is a fantastic form of  squat that you don't see people in the  gym doing and the only reason i can  think for this is because it comes from  ballet and i think that's an awful shame  in a demo plie the aim is to keep your  heels on the ground and just to squat  down as far as you can without letting  those heels raise off the floor in a  ground plie in a full plie you squat  down as far as you can allowing the  heels to come up off the floor but when  you get to the bottom of the movement  you should be going as deep as you  possibly can you're still not going to  rest on the heels you're still going to  be maintaining strength through the feet  in a releve plie you go up into the  balls of your feet and then go all the  way down like that this is fantastic for  actually training the feet themselves  which are brilliant for jumping and even  for jumping with a fully extended leg  you'll train your feet and your calves  which again are massively underutilized  by a lot of people in the gym and this  will help you run faster jump higher  generally perform much better again this  isn't just for looking pretty once again  you want to keep that pelvis tucked  throughout the movement so you have a  nice neutral spine this should help you  to stand tall and maintain your balance  a lot of this mobility comes from  concentrating on the right things and  from relaxing your body and the same  goes for your balance and your general  posture  in fact in order to balance you need to  be relaxed balance is not about strength  it's not about brute forcing yourself  into position in fact being tense is  going to get in your way instead you  need to focus on poise  on aligning your joints on letting  yourself listen to the reflexes of your  body which naturally want to get into  that position of alignment if you listen  to your body if you gain that mobility  and that control you'll naturally be in  a balanced position and it's from that  balanced poised position that you can  exert the most power and performance  another interesting example comes from  the cue to visualize a spring or rocket  while jumping using this simple  visualization technique studies show  that dancers can actually increase their  vertical jump i believe this works like  a form of chunking for the working  memory imagine throwing a punch and  trying to remember everything you've  been taught and a lot of people will  find that their attention and awareness  breaks down in the moment i know mine  does  by using visual cues however you can  help your body to automatically arrange  itself just as a mnemonic can help you  to remember a list of words all this  speaks to the real power of a dancer the  ability to coordinate every part of the  body around one central goal a great  dance looks beautiful because the dancer  is able to control every part of their  body with intent and power  we could be so much stronger and improve  our movement so much simply by being  better aware of our muscles and better  able to control them  got anterior pelvic tilt the solution is  not necessarily just to stretch the hip  flexors but simply to relearn how to  control the pelvis my planche training  has made a lot of progress since i  started simply focusing more on keeping  my arms locked during the pseudo planche  lean that same kind of awareness and  poise can help you in every kind of  movement lately i've been trying to  focus more on performing my exercises so  not just going through the motions but  actually trying to attack the motions  with as much speed and frost as i can  whilst at the same time thinking about  every part of my body is my core braced  am i squeezing my glutes is anything  flapping around or not where it should  be where am i looking focusing on these  things and thinking about it in this way  can improve your proprioception to the  point that you're aware of every part of  your body and where it is in space at  any given time so next time you're  training think a little bit more like a  dancer and you might find that your  movements become that much more deadly  and while she may be a fictional  character it also perfectly explains how  black widow can take down a much larger  opponent by moving fluidly powerfully  and with incredible precision just like  the ocean can break a sheer cliff face  it's nuts to me that we don't see this  kind of training in the gym more  [Music]  and we can combine this with other forms  of spy-like training to build a tactical  functional physique like the tactical  pull-up i talked about recently rope  wall climbs for entering buildings low  crawls for moving close to the ground  parkour rolls and jumps for traversal  carries for moving gear and supplies  endurance training to avoid fatigue long  distance running and sprinting at the  other end of the spectrum and of course  large amounts of combat training and  martial arts  that's how you build a black widow  physique  so thanks a ton for watching guys i hope  you found this video useful and  interesting definitely something a  little bit different today let me know  in the comments how you think black  widow would trade whether you think  there are benefits that you can get from  dance and from ballet in particular and  how they might transfer over to whatever  your chosen activity is the batman  training for 2022 is still on the way  i'm just working on something pretty big  and special for that at the same time  also putting together that montage of  bioneer training so go to the facebook  page and get involved if you want to  submit your videos before that goes live  and there's lots more exciting stuff on  the way if you like the concept of  combining different training styles to  get the very most functionality out of  your workouts and you might enjoy my  ebook and training program super  functional training there's a link to  that in description down below and i  also have a print book out called  functional training and beyond which you  can find at amazon and i'll put a link  to that as well  either way thank you so much for  watching this one guys and i'll see you  next time  bye for now

